pgw and pgwindex, which dict -d pgw reads, are Webster's dictionary of
1913, from Project Gutenberg's text (https://www.gutenberg.org/), with
dict's index. They carry neither Project Gutenberg's license nor its
name.

p9web's scripts/dl.sh fetches them as Plan 9's sources server had them,
from 9p.io's copy, and checks their SHA-256:

	https://9p.io/sources/extra/pgw.tar.bz2

On Plan 9, to get them from sources use

	9fs sources
	cp /n/sources/extra/pgw.tar.bz2 /tmp
	cd /lib/dict
	bunzip2 < /tmp/pgw.tar.bz2 | tar x
